          "pull_request": {
            "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/duckdb-bot/duckdb/pulls/127",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/duckdb-bot/duckdb/pull/127",
            "diff_url": "https://github.com/duckdb-bot/duckdb/pull/127.diff",
            "patch_url": "https://github.com/duckdb-bot/duckdb/pull/127.patch",
            "merged_at": null
          },
          "body": "When Parquet files disagree on a column's type, filtering that column could fail with an error like `Could not convert string 'foo' to INT32`, without identifying the file or column. Selecting the same column already reported the file, column and types, and suggested `union_by_name`. This was reported in duckdb/duckdb#22399.\n\nWhen a filter cannot be cast to a file's column type, the multi-file mapper pushes the column cast into an `ExpressionColumnReader`, so the filter runs on cast values. That bypasses `MultiFileReader::FinalizeChunk`, where errors from projected-column casts receive file context.\n\nThis change shares the hint through `MultiFileReader::GetCastErrorHint` and adds it to cast failures in those readers, leaving internal errors untouched. It also removes a doubled `: `; casts inside `STRUCT` fields still give bare errors. The new regression test fails on main and covers filtering, projection, additional filters across several rows, overflow and `union_by_name`. Parquet and multi-file tests pass. All unit tests pass except `test/sql/aoc24/aoc24.test_slow`, which hit a recursive CTE caching operator INTERNAL error once, then passed on rerun here and on main.\n\nFixes duckdblabs/bot-issue-tracker#176\nRelated: duckdb/duckdb#22399\n",
